# /etc/sudoers.d/dashboard-system-update
#
# A template: scripts/setup-app-account.sh fills in @APP_USER@ (the app's
# own account, which nothing else runs as) and installs it.
#
# Grants the dashboard's Node process passwordless access to exactly the
# system commands it needs — nothing broader:
#   - /usr/local/sbin/family-dashboard-apt, used by scripts/system-update.sh
#     after every self-update to install packages listed in
#     system/packages.txt. It accepts Debian package NAMES only (no apt
#     options, paths or .deb files) — a plain `apt-get install -y *` rule
#     would amount to passwordless root.
#   - the "Exit to Terminal" debug feature (ends the desktop session,
#     which belongs to the desktop login, not the app account)
#
# Deliberately NOT here: installing system/dashboard.service. That file
# lives in the app-writable folder, so letting the app copy it into
# /etc/systemd/system would let it define a root service. Service-file
# changes are applied by re-running scripts/setup-app-account.sh by hand.
#
# Installed by scripts/setup-app-account.sh; checked by scripts/harden-pi.sh.

@APP_USER@ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/sbin/family-dashboard-apt
@APP_USER@ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/pkill -f /usr/lib/xorg/Xorg
@APP_USER@ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/pkill -x labwc
